From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: skip monitor status reap until the ring is initialized

During firmware recovery the extended interrupt groups are re-enabled
before the monitor status refill ring has been set up again. Servicing
the ring in that window passes an uninitialized srng to
ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin() and panics in interrupt context -
observed deterministically on IPQ8074 with NSS offload: every firmware
fatal (hif_ce.c assertion -> Q6 SSR) turned into a host kernel panic
about one second into the recovery, from the napi thread:

  ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin+0xc
  ath11k_dp_rx_process_mon_status+0x15c
  ath11k_dp_service_srng+0xb8
  ath11k_ahb_ext_grp_napi_poll+0x34

Because the panic fires in the recovery path, it converts every
recoverable firmware crash into a reboot.

The monitor status refill ring is a source ring - the reap walks it with
ath11k_hal_srng_src_peek() - so ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin() reads
srng->u.src_ring.tp_addr, and that is the pointer that is NULL here.
Test it directly rather than srng->initialized: ath11k_hal_srng_setup()
sets ->initialized before ->tp_addr and without a barrier, so an
->initialized check can still be true while tp_addr is NULL and would
race the very ring rebuild it is meant to exclude. Same reasoning, and
the same predicate, as the CE guard in 999-929.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
index 9e05860..ab1e5a0 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -3808,6 +3808,20 @@
 	rx_ring = &dp->rx_mon_status_refill_ring[srng_id];
 
 	srng = &ab->hal.srng_list[rx_ring->refill_buf_ring.ring_id];
+
+	/*
+	 * During firmware recovery the extended interrupt groups are
+	 * re-enabled before the monitor status ring is set up again;
+	 * servicing it in that window dereferences an uninitialized srng
+	 * and panics in interrupt context. This is a source ring, so
+	 * ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin() reads u.src_ring.tp_addr - test
+	 * that pointer rather than ->initialized, because
+	 * ath11k_hal_srng_setup() sets ->initialized before ->tp_addr
+	 * without a barrier, leaving an ->initialized check racing the
+	 * ring rebuild it is meant to exclude.
+	 */
+	if (!srng->u.src_ring.tp_addr)
+		return 0;
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&srng->lock);
 
